    "chunk_text": "Malwana student standoff draws PM\u2019s attention\n\nColombo, May 17 (Daily Mirror) - The attention of the Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education Minister, and Prime Minister Dr. Harini Amarasuriya has been drawn to the situation involving a group of university students who have been staying for several days on a land in the Malwana area under the custody of the Dompe Divisional Secretariat.\n\nAccording to official sources, the matter and the students\u2019 demands have been taken up for review at the highest level. A discussion with the relevant parties is scheduled to be held tomorrow (18) at the Prime Minister\u2019s Office under the patronage of Prime Minister Dr. Harini Amarasuriya.\n\nAuthorities said that further action regarding the issue will be determined following the outcome of this meeting."
