    "md5": "f8f89e05fea68b966c525ac993f0f943",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1496,
    "chunk_text": "Classic Travel wins Gold at Malaysia Airlines Trade Elevation Summit\n\nClassic Travel has once again secured top honours at the Malaysia Airlines Trade Elevation Summit 2026, winning the Golden WAU Award and continuing its consecutive run of recognition at the global industry event.\n\nThe awards ceremony, took place on 14th May at Shangri-La in Kota Kinabalu, recognises outstanding global trade partners that continue to strengthen Malaysia Airlines\u2019 international presence and performance.\n\nThe Malaysia Airlines Trade Elevation Summit (TES) has become one of the airline\u2019s key global industry platforms, bringing together over 300 travel agents, and partners, from across multiple international markets.\n\nOrganised in collaboration with the Malaysia Convention and Exhibition Bureau (MYCEB), the summit focuses on strengthening global partnerships, driving tourism growth, and positioning Malaysia as a strategic tourism and aviation hub.\n\nCommenting on the achievement, Sabry Bahaudeen, Director \u2013 Expolanka Leisure Cluster said: \u201cTo continue being recognised over consecutive years at a global platform such as this is incredibly meaningful for us. It reflects the relentless focus our teams place on quality, customer service, and consistently delivering value to both our customers and partners. We are deeply grateful to Malaysia Airlines for this continued recognition and to our teams and stakeholders whose dedication and trust continue to drive our success year after year.\u201d"
  },
