    "chunk_size_bytes": 1857,
    "chunk_text": "Vella earns Great Place To Work Certification Tm, marking a milestone in its people-first journey\n\nColombo, Sri Lanka (6 May, 2026) Vella has been officially certified as a Great Place to Work, marking a significant milestone in the Group\u2019s ongoing journey to build a culture rooted in trust, shared purpose and collective growth. Great Place To Work\u00ae is the global authority on workplace culture, employee experience, and the leadership behaviors proven to deliver market-leading revenue, employee retention and increased innovation.\n\nAchieved on its first attempt, the certification reflects the strength of Vella\u2019s people culture across its diverse portfolio spanning hospitality, adventure, tea, retail, leisure and lifestyle experiences. The Group\u2019s growing portfolio brings together some of Sri Lanka\u2019s most distinctive destination-led brands, from the quiet luxury of 98 Acres Resort & Spa, vibrant energy of Ravana Pool Club, to the adventure appeal of Flying Ravana Adventure Park, Ella Swing and Amber Swing. Its leisure and hospitality footprint further extends to Walaa Kulu and Villa L\u00e9 Maas Tota, while Halp\u00e9 Tea, Halpe Tea Tour, Ceylon Tea Supermarket, Kiri Kopi, and Ceylon Escapade strengthen the Group\u2019s presence across tea, retail, caf\u00e9 culture, and travel experiences. Together, these brands reflect Vella\u2019s vision to create meaningful experiences that celebrate Sri Lanka\u2019s natural beauty, cultural richness and evolving appeal as a world-class destination.\n\nCEB\u2019s Rs. 8.5 bn VRS package signals deeper power sector restructuring\n\nAIA Sri Lanka hosts the annual Company Conference to honour performance, passion and purpose\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
