    "chunk_text": "As developing and least developed countries struggle with rising fuel import bills, hostilities between the US-Israel alliance and Iran show no signs of abating despite peace efforts. While the US, aligned with Israel, expects Iran to concede to its demands, the Islamic Republic\u2014the wronged party\u2014insists on war reparations, lifting sanctions, and unfreezing its assets as conditions to end the conflict. After all, it was the US-Israel axis that triggered the war in contravention of international law. Iran\u2019s position suggests readiness for another round of fighting if US attacks. With both sides upping the ante, much like boxers before a professional encounter, frustration builds across both developing and developed economies as leaders struggle to prevent currency slides and rising hardships for their people."
