    "chunk_text": "21 alleged underworld members deported from Dubai arrive in Sri Lanka\n\nColombo, May 22 (Daily Mirror) - A group of 21 alleged underworld members who were reportedly deported from Dubai arrived in Sri Lanka this morning (22), according to police sources.\n\nThe suspects were brought back to the country on several flights that had been diverted to the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport due to adverse weather conditions affecting operations at Bandaranaike International Airport.\n\nAmong those reportedly deported are individuals identified as \u201cMahawatte Chamara\u201d and \u201cKudu Duminda\u201d, who are alleged to have links to organized criminal activities.\n\nPolice said \u201cMahawatte Chamara\u201d is scheduled to be handed over to the Central Crime Investigation Bureau for further investigations.\n\nAuthorities stated that inquiries are also expected to continue regarding the other suspects who were brought back to the country."
