    "chunk_text": "Sri Lankan Embassy in Kathmandu celebrates International Tea Day 2026\n\nColombo, May 23 (Daily Mirror) - The Embassy of Sri Lanka in Kathmandu celebrated International Tea Day 2026 under the theme \u201c159 Years of Excellence in Ceylon Tea\u201d at the official residence of the Ambassador in Kathmandu.\n\nThe event brought together representatives from the Government of Nepal, tea industry stakeholders and distinguished guests to commemorate the heritage and global reputation of Ceylon Tea.\n\nThe programme commenced with the arrival and registration of guests, followed by the formal opening ceremony and keynote address by Sri Lanka\u2019s Ambassador to Nepal, Ruwanthi Delpitiya.\n\nAddressing the gathering, the Ambassador highlighted the rich heritage and international recognition of Ceylon Tea, noting that the industry marks 159 years of excellence this year. Referring to the International Tea Day 2026 theme, \u201cSustaining Tea, Supporting Communities,\u201d she reaffirmed Sri Lanka\u2019s commitment to sustainability, ethical production practices and the wellbeing of tea-growing communities.\n\nShe further stated that Ceylon Tea remains one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most recognised global brands, reflecting the country\u2019s tradition of quality, authenticity and excellence. The Ambassador also underscored tea\u2019s role as a symbol of hospitality, cultural connection and friendship between Sri Lanka and Nepal.\n\nThe programme also featured presentations on the Food and Agriculture Organization Intergovernmental Group themes for International Tea Day 2026, along with screenings of official campaign visuals and videos.\n\nA presentation on Ceylon Tea was delivered by Embassy Commercial Officer Bibek Wosti, followed by videos showcasing Sri Lanka\u2019s tea heritage, quality standards and export significance."
