    "chunk_size_bytes": 1516,
    "chunk_text": "CBK plays major role inducting Sirisena as common opposition candidate against MR\n\nBy this time MR was coming to the end of his second term. The thoughts of politicians turned to the forthcoming Presidential election particularly because the constitution stipulated only a two term tenure for a President. Also by this time the Rajapaksa family, which played only a minor role when MR first sought the Presidency, had grown to large proportions and were seen to be interfering in the daily management of the country\u2019s affairs.\n\nGotabaya, who had played a crucial role in the war became the Secretary in charge of Urban Development. He performed magnificently turning Colombo and its suburbs into a much more habitable environment. Since there were a large number of demobbed soldiers he used their skills for urban development projects. Modeled on the facilities made available to war veterans in the US he built a defence headquarters, hospitals, Universities, hospices for the disabled and employed many soldiers in related businesses.\n\nIt was a splendid effort and he drew the admiration of the general public for his honesty and efficiency. But others unfortunately got involved in deal making. All in all MR began to lose his popularity due to the shenanigans of his relatives. There was growing dissent largely because Prime Minister Jayaratne was critically ill and MR did not appoint a successor. All these embers of discontent were fanned energetically by CBK who had returned after a long sojourn abroad."
