    "md5": "0172b6516ae417b90fead07e74420d9e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1768,
    "chunk_text": "While enjoying a chit chat in the Parliamentary lobby I was told that CBK and some senior UNPers were zeroing in on Maithripala Sirisena as the possible rebel chief against MR. Sirisena was a popular General Secretary of the party after being promoted by party seniors like DM Jayaratne to contest that post against CBK\u2019s nominee SB Dissanayake. After the successful SB defected to the UNP, he was appointed Secretary of the party and CBK apologized publicly for overlooking him earlier.\n\nOur last meeting was in Bath University in the UK when Mahinda Deegalla who was a teacher there invited me to be a participant in a seminar on modern Buddhism. Among the monks invited for this conference were Sobhita, Athureliye Ratana and a chief monk from Vavuniya. Scholars of modern Buddhism like Gananath Obeyesekere, HL Seneviratne, Ananda Wickremaratne, RALH Gunawardene, Premasiri, Heinz Bechert and Peter Ibbotson were also invited. We had a very interesting four days together and I was able to renew my links with Sobhita.\n\nI took it upon myself to visit the dorm in which the monks were lodged to ensure that they were comfortable. We had meals together and I heard the gossip that they shared with each other. When some monks were embarrassed, Sobhita introduced me as a \u2018safe person\u2019 and the slander of their high priests continued amidst much laughter.\n\nI learnt of the anti-Rajapaksa movement from Rev. Ratana who spoke to me in confidence in the lobby of Parliament. He wanted me as \u201can educated man\u201d to join them in supporting a successor to MR. I declined his offer of changing sides because I had no personal grudge against MR as did the other conspirators. It was also clear at that time that there was no consensus on whom the challenger would be."
