    "chunk_text": "I learnt of the anti-Rajapaksa movement from Rev. Ratana who spoke to me in confidence in the lobby of Parliament. He wanted me as \u201can educated man\u201d to join them in supporting a successor to MR. I declined his offer of changing sides because I had no personal grudge against MR as did the other conspirators. It was also clear at that time that there was no consensus on whom the challenger would be.\n\nThe opposition to MR became strong after he declared that he was seeking a third term as President. He also wanted to hold the election long before its due date. The possibility of a third term was precluded by a provision in our constitution. To circumvent that MR was contemplating introducing an amendment to the constitution to be passed with a two third majority in Parliament. This was a galling situation especially for the left which could not easily accept the Napoleonic ambitions of a President who was fast losing his popularity.\n\nAt meetings of the Central Committee of the SLFP this matter was taken up. But our feeble protests were overridden by the MR faction. The Communist Party led by DEW Gunasekera protested and threatened to vote against the amendment in Parliament. The LSSP and Vasudeva remained silent and when presented in Parliament the amendment was passed but in time proved it to be a pyrrhic victory. However we have to admit that our reluctant vote for this aberration is an unforgivable black mark in our Parliamentary record."
  },
