    "chunk_text": "At meetings of the Central Committee of the SLFP this matter was taken up. But our feeble protests were overridden by the MR faction. The Communist Party led by DEW Gunasekera protested and threatened to vote against the amendment in Parliament. The LSSP and Vasudeva remained silent and when presented in Parliament the amendment was passed but in time proved it to be a pyrrhic victory. However we have to admit that our reluctant vote for this aberration is an unforgivable black mark in our Parliamentary record.\n\nBut unexpectedly fate played a hand. Maitri\u2019s son had gone on a holiday to Passikudah and had been embroiled in an altercation with the son of a DIG. The Police had thrown the book at the young man and Maitri had to rush to Passikudah to save his son. Maitri was treated badly by the local police and the media followed up with a coverage that painted his son as the offender. He believed that Basil Rajapaksa was behind this episode and particularly that the media assault was directed by him. At this stage he contacted me and asked me to intercede with Derana TV network to give a fair coverage of this misadventure and not pillory his son. This unexpected event resulted in his pledge to CBK that he would go forward as the anti-Rajapaksa candidate.\n\nBut other problems still remained. The Tamil parties said that they did not know enough about Maitri to wholeheartedly endorse him. Ranil did not know him well either and raised a query as to whether he could be trusted to follow their policies as President. At this stage CBK put her reputation on the line and declared that \u201cIf they trusted her they should trust Maitri on her guarantee\u201d. It was a guarantee that she came to regret later. Anyway the opposition to MR had found a credible candidate with a strong local base in the North Central Province who could carry the fight to the incumbent who was too good a politician not to know that he was now in trouble."
