    "chunk_size_bytes": 646,
    "chunk_text": "Engine of Hikkaduwa-bound express train derails at Maradana\n\nColombo, May 24 (Daily Mirror) - The engine of the daily express train scheduled to travel from Maradana to Hikkaduwa at 6:10 PM derailed this evening (24) at the Maradana Railway Station.\n\nAccording to reports, the derailment occurred near the Maradana bridge as the locomotive was moving from the yard to couple with the passenger carriages parked at the platform.\n\nFour wheels of the engine slipped off the tracks during the incident. As a result, one of the main railway lines between Maradana and Colombo Fort has been completely blocked, leading to disruptions in train services."
