    "md5": "f2c20dad07bb5ff6c22b6d55d53e58bd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1275,
    "chunk_text": "KIU University tops ministry-led review in higher education\n\nKIU University has set a new benchmark in Sri Lankan higher education by achieving an 85.86% score in the latest Ministry-led Periodic Institutional Review, the highest among non-state universities. This accomplishment is notable as KIU, a relatively young institution, outperformed many long-established universities across six key pillars including governance, academic planning, and quality assurance.\n\nAt the programme level, KIU\u2019s BSc (Hons) in Biomedical Science earned an outstanding 93.7%, among Sri Lanka\u2019s highest-rated programmes, while its Psychology degree scored 83.78%. Programmes in Accounting, Marketing, and HRM also exceeded national standards.\n\nAccredited by the Ministry and recognised by the University Grants Commission (UGC), KIU aligns its offerings with the Sri Lanka Qualifications Framework. The university\u2019s graduates have secured overseas postgraduate scholarships and demonstrated strong employability.\n\nBuilding a reliable Web3 talent pool: Sri Lanka\u2019s strategic leap in South Asia\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
