    "md5": "83c4266ebe31952f73f2be0f27b1fc85",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 976,
    "chunk_text": "Day and postponement Vesak 2026\n\nMay Day can mean one of many things. In European countries it is a festival, dating back nearly a thousand years, celebrating the beginning of the summer. People across the UK, especially in villages, hold fetes on 1st of May, celebrating May Day in different ways including maypole dancing, Morris dancing and the crowning of a May Queen. In many other countries it is a celebration of the International Labour Day, its origin dating back to the 1886 Haymarket Affair in Chicago where workers striking for an eight-hour day faced violent suppression, resulting in many deaths and the execution of some labour leaders. Sri Lanka is among around 80 countries celebrating this event of worker\u2019s solidarity though it has become highly politicised, unfortunately.\n\nOn the other hand, \u2018mayday\u2019 repeated thrice, is the universal call sign for distress used by aviators and sailors, other emergency services too adopting this in some countries."
