    "chunk_text": "What transpired at the government May Day rallies raises the spectre of a mayday, no doubt!\u00a0 However, what is not sure is whether the danger is to the government or to the electoral process. Perhaps, it is for both, as a failing government may look for alternatives to democracy. Wonder whether the words of Tilvin Silva, the power behind the throne, would turn out to be prophetic. Addressing one of the many NPP May Day rallies, he proclaimed to the applause of his supporters that there would be no future governments. After a pause he added that the opposition does not know how to form a government. Whether he did so to soften the blow or on the realisation that he had dropped a clanger, we do not know!\n\nThe NPP\u2019s victory was mainly on the promise of good governance but their actions. Just like their predecessors, whom they criticised heavily, they seem to go all out to defend their corrupt colleagues. The rot started with the appointment of the Speaker who claimed to have a doctorate. But he is still an MP! Replacement seems no better, if what is rumoured is true.\n\nAKD promised the abolition of the presidency, but rather than honouring that promise, he seems hell-bent on heading towards a dictatorship. He is chasing after political enemies using the Seneviratna Abeysekara duo, pulled out of retirement to be installed in high positions, in spite of pending allegations! Either, he does not understand the concept of the separation of the executive, legislature and the judiciary for good governance or has taken it for granted. During May Day celebrations, AKD told his supporters to wait to cheer when a judgement is given in a corruption case where a directive has been issued to hand over the verdict within a month. This led to heavy criticism from the opposition and a belated response from BASL but usually vociferous AKD remains silent!"
