    "chunk_text": "AKD promised the abolition of the presidency, but rather than honouring that promise, he seems hell-bent on heading towards a dictatorship. He is chasing after political enemies using the Seneviratna Abeysekara duo, pulled out of retirement to be installed in high positions, in spite of pending allegations! Either, he does not understand the concept of the separation of the executive, legislature and the judiciary for good governance or has taken it for granted. During May Day celebrations, AKD told his supporters to wait to cheer when a judgement is given in a corruption case where a directive has been issued to hand over the verdict within a month. This led to heavy criticism from the opposition and a belated response from BASL but usually vociferous AKD remains silent!\n\nA government that came to power, raising the expectations of the public extremely high, seems to be failing. If there is a change of government, there is a great likelihood that many in the ranks of this government too may join the corrupt in jail, as this government lost the promised squeaky-clean image quite a while ago.\n\nThere are rumours that the government is hunting for talent in the ranks of the opposition, not something expected of a government that claims to have walking encyclopaedias of every description in its ranks!\n\nIn this scenario, the million-dollar question is whether the government would do everything possible not to have elections. Will it be \u201cmayday, mayday, mayday\u201d for democracy?\n\nTOXIC WATERS: How Galle\u2019s rivers are becoming invisible hotspots for superbugs and disease risk\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
