    "md5": "6e75056a562d78ef78732376ec827e88",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1751,
    "chunk_text": "Kelly Felder opens Melbourne flagship store\n\nKelly Felder, Sri Lanka\u2019s leading high-street fashion brand, has officially arrived in Australia, with the grand opening of its Melbourne flagship store at The Glen Shopping Centre, Glen Waverley, recently, making history as the first Sri Lankan fashion brand to establish a retail presence in the Western market.\n\nThe store places Kelly Felder alongside globally recognised names including H&M, UNIQLO and Cotton On, bringing the brand\u2019s signature lifestyle experience to a new international audience.\n\nInside, Kelly Felder\u2019s world unfolds across womenswear, menswear, athleisure, accessories and fragrances, each piece a reflection of the brand\u2019s core belief: that style should make every customer feel confident, elevated and ready for whatever the day demands.\n\nFrom boardrooms to brunches, nights out to quiet mornings, the collections are built for the full spectrum of a modern lifestyle.\n\nThe opening drew an enthusiastic crowd from day one, with Australian-based influencers, fashion personalities and members of Melbourne\u2019s Sri Lankan community coming together to celebrate the arrival of a brand they have long called their own.\n\n\u201cWhat began as an idea in an MBA classroom, inspired while traveling through New York, has evolved into reality with the opening of Kelly Felder\u2019s first international store in Melbourne, a proud milestone in the journey of building a Sri Lankan-based premium lifestyle brand for the world,\u201d said Kelly Felder founder Ravi Wickramanayake.\n\n\u201cThis is a major milestone for us and we are only getting started. Our focus now is on building aggressively, expanding globally and dominating the market,\u201d said Kelly Felder Director Dinith Wickramanayake."
  },
