    "md5": "584728bdaa8dc5c51be4f7f6aae31528",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1907,
    "chunk_text": "SLASSCOM supports AIA\u2019s Mind \u2022 Body \u2022 Soul Wellness Series\n\nAIA Insurance Lanka Chief Marketing Officer Sasith Bambaradeniya and SLASSCOM Chairperson Shehani Seneviratne with AIA and SLASSCOM teams\n\nSLASSCOM has partnered with AIA Insurance as the official Wellness Partner for its flagship Mind \u2022 Body \u2022 Soul Wellness Series 2026, strengthening SLASSCOM\u2019s efforts to champion healthier, more connected workplaces across Sri Lanka\u2019s knowledge and innovation industry.\n\nThis collaboration marks an important step in advancing employee experience and workplace culture across Sri Lanka\u2019s rapidly growing knowledge and innovation industry. It reflects a shared vision to create environments where mental agility, physical wellness and creative expression are recognised as essential parts of building resilient and high-performing teams.\n\nThe Mind \u2022 Body \u2022 Soul series is structured around three signature initiatives designed to support workforce resilience and employee engagement across the industry.\n\nMega Mind will focus on sharpening cognitive ability, problem-solving and mental agility through knowledge-driven engagement experiences. Fit Hit promotes healthier lifestyles through fitness challenges, wellness activities and its flagship 5KM run. Ctrl Alt Rock brings teams together through music, performance and creative expression, creating space for expression, connection and shared experiences beyond the workplace.\n\nThrough this partnership, AIA Insurance joins SLASSCOM in promoting a broader approach to workplace wellness, recognising the growing importance of employee well-being in building stronger organisations and sustainable workplace cultures.\n\nAt a time when organisations are increasingly focused on employee engagement, burnout, retention and workplace culture, the partnership signals a broader shift towards more people-centric workplaces across the industry."
  },
