    "language": "en",
    "md5": "450d41610dfb8b4e2c915566aab80f81",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1529,
    "chunk_text": "MullenLowe\u2019s Sampath Karunaratne awarded Next-Gen Leader Scholarship to Cannes Lions\n\nSampath Karunaratne receives Next-Gen Leader Scholarship from Sysco LABS Director Brand and Communications Gian de Rose in the presence of Metal Factor founder Ranil de Silva\n\nMullenLowe Group Sri Lanka continues its creative dominance as Creative Director Sampath Karunaratne has been named the recipient of the 2026 Next Generation Leader Scholarship to attend the Cannes Lions International Festival of Creativity in France.\n\nThis marks the second consecutive year that a MullenLowe Sri Lanka creative leader has been selected for the scholarship, following Harendra Uyanage, who was recognised as the inaugural recipient last year during his tenure as Vice President and Executive Creative Director.\n\nInitiated by Metal Factor, the  scholarship honours the legacy of Yong Lye Peng and is designed to identify and support emerging leaders within Sri Lanka\u2019s marketing communications industry.\n\nThe programme places a strong emphasis on global exposure, enabling the recipients to engage with leading thinkers, participate in workshops and return with perspectives that can elevate the local industry.\n\nThe 2026 recipient was selected through a rigorous adjudication process led by a distinguished panel comprising Metal Factor Founder Ranil de Silva, Sysco LABS Director Brand and Communications Gian de Rose, DFCC Bank Vice President and Chief Marketing Officer Kaushala Amarasekara and Ngage Strategic Alliance CEO Sheron Jayasundara."
  },
