    "md5": "46e60373a61cc167506d81fef4df6428",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1446,
    "chunk_text": "The 2026 recipient was selected through a rigorous adjudication process led by a distinguished panel comprising Metal Factor Founder Ranil de Silva, Sysco LABS Director Brand and Communications Gian de Rose, DFCC Bank Vice President and Chief Marketing Officer Kaushala Amarasekara and Ngage Strategic Alliance CEO Sheron Jayasundara.\n\nKarunaratne brings nearly two decades of experience in Sri Lanka\u2019s advertising industry, having begun his career as a copywriter and steadily built a reputation for creative excellence and leadership. The scholarship provides him with a partially funded opportunity to attend the 2026 festival and engage with the global creative community.\n\nReflecting on the recognition, Karunaratne said, \u201cI see this opportunity as a responsibility to take Sri Lankan creativity to the world. Not just to participate but to show that we belong on that stage and to create more opportunities for others to follow.\u201d\n\nMullenLowe Group Sri Lanka Vice President and Chief Creative Officer Harendra Uyanage added, \u201cSampath\u2019s journey reflects a deep commitment to creative excellence and to the teams he has led over the years and this recognition is well deserved, speaking to both his craft and his leadership. Exposure to the Cannes Lions International Festival of Creativity will add a new dimension to his thinking and I am confident he will return with insights that will contribute meaningfully to our industry.\u201d"
