    "chunk_size_bytes": 1810,
    "chunk_text": "Basilur Tea marks Int\u2019l Tea Day with Roots of Ceylon launch\n\nThe Sri Lankan premium Ceylon Tea brand, Basilur Tea, launched the Roots of Ceylon initiative in celebration of the International Tea Day, inviting the tea enthusiasts to tie into the rich history of Ceylon Tea.\n\nWith 202 years having passed since the first tea plants arrived in Sri Lanka, this year\u2019s celebration marked a significant milestone in tea history and culture. Through the Roots of Ceylon initiative, Basilur Tea planted 202 new tea plants as an ode to the industry that took the flavours of Ceylon Tea to the world.\n\nGuided by its philanthropic values, the Roots of Ceylon initiative was focused on the intention of bringing communities across the globe together. This campaign connected tea connoisseurs who adore Basilur Tea to Sri Lanka\u2019s rich tea heritage.\n\nBasilur Tea Export Chairman Dr. Gamini Abeywickrama said, \u201cThis year, the International Tea Day holds great significance, as it also marks 202 years since tea plants were first brought to the nation. Roots of Ceylon allowed us to honour our vibrant history and culture while welcoming a new chapter of tea with our consumers. Remembering Ceylon\u2019s legacy and having the opportunity to be part of that story is incredibly special to all of us.\u201d\n\nInspired by the International Tea Day theme \u2018Fostering Growth and Inclusion\u2019, the Roots of Ceylon initiative was created to enrich Sri Lanka\u2019s tea industry for the next generation.\n\nDr. Abeywickrama, joined by Managing Director Thushari Abeywickrama and their sons Finance Director Rajitha Abeywickrama and Marketing Director Charaka Abeywickrama as well as Basilur Tea estate workers and their children, took part in the planting ceremony of the Roots of Ceylon initiative at the Bucsh Tea Estate in Baddegama."
