    "chunk_text": "Kumar Sangakkara throws weight behind Parag amid criticism\n\nKumar Sangakkara has thrown his support behind Riyan Parag, insisting the young captain remains the right leader for Rajasthan Royals despite heavy criticism during IPL 2026.\n\nSpeaking after RR\u2019s 30-run win over Mumbai Indians at the Wankhede Stadium on Sunday, Sangakkara praised Parag\u2019s leadership and the respect he commands inside the dressing room.\n\n\u201cI\u2019ve seen very few players criticised like Riyan has been over the last seven years,\u201d Sangakkara said. \u201cBut when we decided to give him the captaincy, he was absolutely the right guy to lead this franchise.\u201d\n\nParag has scored 272 runs this season at a strike rate of 152.80, with only two half-centuries in his first year as RR\u2019s full-time captain. Despite his struggles with the bat, Sangakkara said the 24-year-old had handled the role with maturity and confidence.\n\n\u201cHe will grow, mature and understand himself and his players even better,\u201d Sangakkara said. \u201cHe\u2019s captained exceptionally well and has the respect of all the players and staff.\u201d\n\nParag returned against MI after missing the previous game with a hamstring injury and scored a quick 14 off eight balls as RR posted 205 for 8 and sealed a playoff spot for the second time in three seasons.\n\nSangakkara also defended RR\u2019s tactical move to send Jofra Archer ahead of specialist batter Shubham Dubey during the innings. Archer responded with a blazing 32 off 15 balls \u2014 his highest IPL score.\n\n\u201cIf we had pushed another batter, we would have had to bowl four overs of Dasun Shanaka,\u201d Sangakkara explained. \u201cOn a wicket like this, that would have been tough.\u201d\n\nHe added that RR delayed bringing in Ravindra Jadeja as an Impact Player due to injury concerns.\n\n\u201cHe\u2019s been nursing an injury, so we\u2019ve had to manage him carefully,\u201d Sangakkara said. \u201cThe way he batted today was exceptional.\u201d"
