    "md5": "1339da2224aecd8ed5932441e00361e3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1670,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka tells Vietnam: Stable, reformed economy ready for capital\n\nBOI Acting Chairman Dr. Sulakshana Jayawardena addressing the Sri Lanka\u2013Vietnam Trade, Investment and Tourism Cooperation Forum\n\nBOI Acting Chairman Dr. Sulakshana Jayawardena unveils 30 structured investment projects in multiple sectors\n\nManufacturing and export processing projects include apparel, electronics assembly, rubber products, dairy processing, pharmaceuticals, textiles and EV assembly\n\nLogistics and port-related pipeline spans Colombo Port logistics hubs, warehousing, Customs facilities and aircraft MRO operations at Mattala\n\nTourism investment opportunities include heritage hotels, theme parks, recreational hubs and cruise tourism projects\n\nInfrastructure and mixed development pipeline covers techno parks, cinema city projects, residential apartments and integrated urban developments\n\n\u201cSri Lanka is open for business,\u201d was the unambiguous message Board of Investment (BOI) of Sri Lanka Acting Chairman Dr. Sulakshana Jayawardena delivered to an audience of Vietnamese business leaders and officials at the Sri Lanka\u2013Vietnam Trade, Investment and Tourism Cooperation Forum on 8 Ma.\n\nAfter weathering one of the most severe economic crises in its post-independence history, Dr. Jayawardena told delegates the island nation has emerged with renewed macroeconomic stability, restored investor confidence, and a clearly articulated vision for growth.\n\nHis case for why international investors \u2014 particularly those from Vietnam and Southeast Asia \u2014 should look seriously at Sri Lanka was built on data, policy, and a pipeline of 30 project-ready investment opportunities."
  },
