    "md5": "73a1609f426900d9b955627a4ef9f822",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1502,
    "chunk_text": "Dr. Rohitha Silva appointed FCCISL President\n\nDr. Rohitha Silva has been appointed President of the Federation of Chambers of Commerce and Industry of Sri Lanka (FCCISL), one of the country\u2019s leading apex business organisations representing 63 chambers countrywide trade associations, entrepreneurs, regional business communities and private-sector stakeholders.\n\nHis appointment comes at a critical time when Sri Lankan entrepreneurs and businesses are still recovering from multiple crises conditions, including COVID-19, foreign exchange shortages, inflation, high finance costs, supply chain disruptions, labour shortages and weak market confidence. Many SMEs continue to face pressure in daily operations, working capital, delayed payments, rising overheads and sustaining employment and productivity.\n\nWith more than 35 years of business experience, Dr. Silva is expected to bring practical leadership, private-sector understanding and international exposure to the Federation. He is Chairman and Managing Director of idac Ltd., a company engaged in total solutions for air conditioning and ventilation.\n\nDr. Silva has served FCCISL for many years in several important capacities, including Board Member, Director, Vice President, Strategy Committee Chairman and member of many committees. Through these roles, he has contributed to strengthening the chamber movement, supporting entrepreneurship, promoting policy dialogue and improving business representation at regional and national levels."
