    "chunk_size_bytes": 1733,
    "chunk_text": "Rooso Ramachandran appointed Global CEO of EFL Global\n\nEFL Global, a member of the SG Holdings Group, a leading Japanese comprehensive global logistics group, announced the appointment of Rooso Ramachandran as the new Global Chief Executive Officer of EFL Global, marking an important leadership transition as part of a broader organizational realignment aimed at strengthening global integration and improving execution across markets.\n\nRooso assumes the role with deep institutional knowledge of EFL Global; A global supply chain and logistics solutions company providing integrated services across transportation, warehousing, distribution, customs brokerage, and compliance. Operating through 100+ offices in 39 countries, EFL Global combines local expertise with global reach to simplify logistics through agile and customer-focused solutions.\n\nHaving spent 24 years building the company\u2019s India business into a profitable and strategically important operation, Rooso has led commercial development, business strategy, operations and administration, while cultivating long-standing partnerships with several of the company\u2019s key global clients.\n\nHe has also played a significant role in expanding EFL Global\u2019s capabilities across high-growth verticals such as pharmaceuticals, automotive and perishables, helping the business respond to evolving customer needs and market opportunities.\n\nWith a strong understanding of EFL Global\u2019s operating model, culture and strategic priorities, Rooso brings proven leadership experience across multiple phases of the company\u2019s growth. In his new role, he will focus on stabilizing performance, strengthening execution and positioning the business for sustainable long-term growth."
