    "md5": "0e9141473e1e0581c11147dfc1584fb0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1735,
    "chunk_text": "KTM Peliyagoda brings premium motorcycles closer to riders\n\nNaalaka Madugalle along with Lakmal de Silva, Akila Elabodage cutting the ribbon to open KTM Peliyagoda.\n\nNaalaka Madugalle handing over the bike key to one of first customers\n\nFurther strengthening the presence of KTM motorcycles in Sri Lanka following their reintroduction by David Pieris Motor Company (Private) Limited (DPMC), the latest showroom, KTM Peliyagoda, was recently opened at No. 389, Negombo Road.\n\nNaalaka Madugalle, Director and Chief Operating Officer, David Pieris Motor Company (Private) Limited along with Lakmal de Silva, Chief Officer \u2013 Vehicle Sales, Akila Elabodage, Divisional Manager \u2013 Vehicle Sales declared opened the new dealer showroom.\n\nThe new state-of-the-art showroom offers motorcycle enthusiasts the opportunity to experience KTM\u2019s globally renowned range of performance motorcycles, including the Duke 160, Duke 250 and Adventure 390 X models.\n\nDPMC officially reintroduced KTM motorcycles to Sri Lanka earlier this year after a five-year hiatus, once again enabling local riders to experience one of the world\u2019s leading high-performance motorcycle brands.\n\nGlobally recognised as Europe\u2019s No. 1 racing motorcycle brand, KTM has established a dominant presence in premier international racing arenas including MotoGP, the Dakar Rally, motocross championships and leading global racing circuits. The brand also enjoys strong popularity across regional markets such as India and Nepal, while maintaining a footprint in more than 80 countries worldwide. KTM\u2019s rich racing heritage, engineering excellence and consistent track performance have earned the trust of professional riders and motorcycle enthusiasts around the globe."
