    "md5": "7bfa4a0373c13d2825bef6fc5738905f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1785,
    "chunk_text": "Pelwatte to invest Rs.1.86bn in liquid milk plant in Kurunegala\n\nPelwatte Dairy Industries said it would invest Rs.1.86 billion in a new liquid milk manufacturing facility in Kurunegala, as the company seeks to expand into value-added dairy products while supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s push to strengthen local food security and nutrition.\n\nThe investment will be made through its fully-owned subsidiary Pelwatte Foods (Private) Limited, under an agreement signed with the Board of Investment (BOI) on May 21.\n\nThe Greenfield facility, expected to begin construction in July 2026, with commercial operations targeted by July 2027, will produce liquid milk and flavoured milk beverages including chocolate, vanilla, strawberry and iced coffee variants.\n\nThe move comes as Sri Lanka continues to grapple with persistent malnutrition concerns, particularly among the mothers and children, despite the improvements in macroeconomic stability.\n\nAccording to global and national health estimates cited by the company, nearly one in six babies in Sri Lanka is born with low birth weight, while around 17 percent of children under five are stunted and over 15 percent suffer from wasting.\n\nPelwatte said the new plant, which would feature automated processing technology and modern manufacturing systems, is expected to strengthen the domestic dairy production capacity and reduce reliance on imported dairy products.\n\nThe investment also reflects a broader shift by the local dairy producers towards higher-value and ready-to-consume nutrition products as consumer demand evolves.\n\nAlthough the project is expected to generate limited direct employment, due to its automated nature, the company said it would support the wider dairy ecosystem by increasing the demand for locally sourced raw milk."
