    "md5": "d35e9bbce49342372e3c2bdfe0596195",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1539,
    "chunk_text": "Women MPs appoint subcommittee on Anuradhapura child abuse case\n\nThe Women Parliamentarians\u2019 Caucus has appointed a sub-committee to oversee future legal proceedings related to the alleged child sexual abuse incident reported from Anuradhapura and to recommend institutional and legal reforms focused at eliminating violence against women and children.\n\nThe decision was taken during a meeting of the Women Parliamentarians\u2019 Caucus Chaired by Minister Saroja Savithri Paulraj at Parliament yesterday.\n\nThe subcommittee will be led by Deputy Co-Chairs of the Caucus, MPs Samanmali Gunasinghe and Chamindrani Kiriella.\n\nOther members appointed to the subcommittee include; Hemali Weerasekara, Dr. Kaushalya Ariyarathna, Sagarika Athauda, Nilanthi Kottahachchi, Nilusha Lakmali Gamage, Thushari Jayasinghe, Anushka Thilakarathna, Hasara Liyanage, Hiruni Wijesinghe and Lakmali Hemachandra.\n\nDuring the meeting, the Caucus also decided to examine the ongoing legal proceedings and matters relating to the protection of the girl involved in the incident, which has drawn significant public attention.\n\nAccordingly, a special discussion has been scheduled for 5 June, with the participation of the Sri Lanka Police, the Attorney General\u2019s Department, the National Child Protection Authority (NCPA) and the Department of Probation and Child Care Services.\n\nThe discussion is expected to focus on the progress of the case as well as measures to strengthen laws and institutions responsible for preventing violence against women and children."
  },
