    "description": "AG to file indictments against Deshabandu within month over \u2018Aragalaya\u2019 attack probe",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/news/AG-to-file-indictments-against-Deshabandu-within-month-over-Aragalaya-attack-probe/56-792507",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1779838840.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-05-27-dailyftlk-ebc9e1b4-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "1d9cac446d2759a391bd147b750461cf",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1388,
    "chunk_text": "AG to file indictments against Deshabandu within month over \u2018Aragalaya\u2019 attack probe\n\nThe Attorney General has informed the Supreme Court of Sri Lanka that indictments are expected to be filed within one month against former Inspector General of Police Deshabandu Thennakoon in connection with investigations into the 2022 attack on Aragalaya protesters at Galle Face Green.\n\nThe disclosure was made on Monday during the hearing of an appeal filed by the Attorney General challenging a Court of Appeal ruling that quashed a directive issued to the Criminal Investigation Department to name Thennakoon as a suspect in the case.\n\nThe matter was heard before a three-judge bench comprising Justices A.H.M.D. Nawaz, Achala Wengappuli and Sampath Wijeratne.\n\nDeputy Solicitor General Suharshi Herath, appearing for the Attorney General, informed Court that steps would be taken to file indictments against Thennakoon within one month.\n\nChief Justice Nawaz, who presided over the bench, questioned how long the process would take before the Deputy Solicitor General provided the timeline.\n\nSenior Counsel Romesh de Silva, appearing for Thennakoon, submitted that if indictments were filed against his client, the continuation of the present proceedings would become invalid.\n\nFollowing submissions by both parties, the Supreme Court fixed the matter for further hearing on 2 September 2026."
  },
