    "md5": "022517255f6882ffdcb74f741244b27b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1698,
    "chunk_text": "Initially entering the global market as a bulk tea exporter, ADRA Ceylon has built a strong foundation through its steadfast adherence to exemplary product quality, consistency, and strategic market expansion. Over the years, the company has progressively amplified its business model with a focus on value-added tea products to enhance brand presence and capture greater value within global markets.\n\nADRA Ceylon\u2019s early years were characterised by rapid market penetration, followed by expanded brand development initiatives and substantial growth in value-added tea segments, positioning the company among the leading exporters of Ceylon tea to the region. Following its consolidation and entry into the export sector, the company rapidly expanded into the East Asian market by establishing a branch office in Taiwan during its second year of operations.In its 10th year of operations, ADRA Ceylon successfully penetrated the highly competitive Gulf, UK, and French markets, further strengthening the company\u2019s presence across the Gulf region and Europe.\n\nDirector \u2013 Tea Indika Abeywickrama said, \u201cADRA Ceylon\u2019s expansion over the past ten years reflects a meticulously executed global strategy. These achievements in global development have garnered industry recognition, including an honour at the NCE Export Awards in October 2019 for craft and commitment, a testament to ADRA\u2019s unyielding commitment.\u201d\n\nThe company\u2019s international success is underpinned by several core strengths developed over its first decade. Meticulous sourcing from Sri Lanka\u2019s renowned tea regions, coupled with a rigorous \u201cleaf to cup\u201d quality control process ensures consistent premium quality."
  },
