    "md5": "ed7486167a0a8a780cb70dcb5209f873",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1872,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s PayPal journey\n\nThe global financial industry is undergoing one of the most profound transformations in modern economic history. Rapid technological advancement, digital innovation, artificial intelligence, and evolving consumer expectations are fundamentally changing the way individuals and businesses conduct financial transactions.\n\nAmong the most influential developments in this transformation is the rise of digital payment platforms such as PayPal, which has revolutionised online financial services across the world.\n\nAs the global economy becomes increasingly dependent on digital commerce, electronic transactions, and remote business operations, Sri Lanka is steadily moving toward deeper integration with international digital payment systems.\n\nThe expansion of PayPal services represents a significant milestone in the country\u2019s journey toward a more connected, innovative, and globally competitive financial ecosystem. Beyond technological modernisation, this transition opens new opportunities for entrepreneurship, financial inclusion, international trade, and economic growth.\n\nFor decades, traditional commercial banks dominated the financial services industry through branch banking, wire transfers, remittance services, payment settlements, card operations, and international banking activities. Customers relied heavily on physical bank branches and conventional procedures to conduct both domestic and cross-border financial transactions.\n\nHowever, the emergence of Financial Technology (FinTech) has dramatically reshaped the competitive landscape. FinTech companies have introduced faster, more efficient, and customer-centric alternatives to traditional banking services. Digital platforms now enable users to conduct transactions instantly through internet-connected devices, reducing dependence on conventional banking channels."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
