    "language": "en",
    "md5": "6ab917299a3b477da8ed785af1df6041",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1778,
    "chunk_text": "However, the emergence of Financial Technology (FinTech) has dramatically reshaped the competitive landscape. FinTech companies have introduced faster, more efficient, and customer-centric alternatives to traditional banking services. Digital platforms now enable users to conduct transactions instantly through internet-connected devices, reducing dependence on conventional banking channels.\n\nPayPal has emerged as one of the world\u2019s leading online payment systems, allowing individuals and businesses to send and receive money securely over the internet. Functioning as a digital wallet, the platform acts as an intermediary between buyers and sellers during online transactions.\n\nInstead of directly sharing debit or credit card details with merchants, users can complete payments through PayPal, enhancing transaction security, convenience, and protection against online fraud.\n\nThe platform is designed with simplicity and accessibility in mind. Users create accounts using an email address and password, then connect their accounts to bank accounts, debit cards, or credit cards. During online purchases, customers can select PayPal as their preferred payment method and complete transactions securely within seconds.\n\nBusinesses and merchants can also establish commercial accounts to receive payments, process online sales, transfer funds to bank accounts, and manage international transactions efficiently.\n\nGlobally, PayPal is widely used for: Online shopping; Freelance services; Subscription payments; International money transfers; E-commerce transactions; Digital marketplace operations.\n\nIts ability to support multiple currencies and facilitate cross-border transactions has made PayPal one of the most trusted digital payment platforms in the global economy."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
