    "md5": "14e6bf8c0966612e9f161a7cdb5cc4e0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1948,
    "chunk_text": "Globally, PayPal is widely used for: Online shopping; Freelance services; Subscription payments; International money transfers; E-commerce transactions; Digital marketplace operations.\n\nIts ability to support multiple currencies and facilitate cross-border transactions has made PayPal one of the most trusted digital payment platforms in the global economy.\n\nThe increasing participation of Sri Lankan professionals in global freelancing platforms and digital marketplaces has intensified the need for broader PayPal integration within the country\u2019s financial infrastructure.\n\nHistorically, Sri Lankan users faced limitations in receiving payments directly through PayPal due to operational and regulatory restrictions. Although some payment functionalities were available, restrictions on receiving funds created barriers for individuals and businesses involved in international digital commerce. However, the rapid expansion of the digital economy and remote work culture has reinforced the importance of modernising Sri Lanka\u2019s payment infrastructure and strengthening its global digital connectivity.\n\nThe broader integration of PayPal services could create substantial economic opportunities for Sri Lanka.\n\nEmpowering freelancers and digital professionals: Freelancers working in information technology, software engineering, graphic design, digital marketing, online consulting, and content creation would gain easier access to international clients and foreign income streams. This would not only increase individual earnings but also contribute positively to foreign exchange inflows and national economic development.\n\nSupporting SMEs and entrepreneurship: Small and medium-sized enterprises engaged in e-commerce could expand their global customer base through secure and efficient online payment systems. Entrepreneurs would be able to market products and services internationally without depending on complex banking arrangements."
  },
