    "chunk_size_bytes": 1656,
    "chunk_text": "Supporting SMEs and entrepreneurship: Small and medium-sized enterprises engaged in e-commerce could expand their global customer base through secure and efficient online payment systems. Entrepreneurs would be able to market products and services internationally without depending on complex banking arrangements.\n\nAdvancing financial inclusion: Digital payment systems also contribute to greater financial inclusion by enabling individuals and businesses to participate more actively in the global economy, regardless of geographical limitations.\n\nBenefits to banking sector: Contrary to the perception that FinTech solely threatens traditional banking, PayPal integration can also create strategic opportunities for commercial banks.\n\nBanks can benefit from: Increased electronic transaction volumes; Higher debit and credit card usage Foreign exchange transactions; Partnerships with global digital payment providers Enhanced customer engagement through digital services.\n\nInterestingly, PayPal indirectly increases card-based transactions because most accounts are linked to commercial bank accounts and payment cards. As a result, banks continue to generate revenue from electronic payment activity while expanding their digital banking footprint.\n\nSecurity, convenience, and global accessibility: One of PayPal\u2019s strongest advantages is its advanced security framework. The platform uses encryption technologies, fraud monitoring systems, and buyer protection mechanisms that help reduce unauthorised transactions and online financial fraud.\n\nThis robust security infrastructure has significantly strengthened consumer trust and global acceptance."
