    "chunk_id": "2026-05-27-dailyftlk-17312333-0005",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "eaa3f7df7708b26bee6477bd1e81c755",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1941,
    "chunk_text": "In developing economies, disparities in internet access and digital awareness may limit the full benefits of financial technology integration. Therefore, strengthening digital infrastructure and improving public financial literacy remain essential priorities.\n\nIn response, traditional banks worldwide have accelerated digital transformation initiatives by introducing: Internet banking systems; Mobile banking applications; QR payment technologies; Digital wallets; Contactless payment systems; Real-time fund transfer platforms.\n\nThis demonstrates how FinTech innovation is reshaping\u2014not necessarily replacing\u2014the banking sector.\n\nAn important global trend has been the growing collaboration between traditional financial institutions and FinTech companies.\n\nMany commercial banks now partner with digital payment providers to improve: Operational efficiency; Technological innovation; Customer experience; Service delivery.\n\nThese partnerships allow banks to remain competitive while adapting to the demands of a rapidly evolving digital financial marketplace.\n\nDespite the opportunities, digital payment platforms also present serious challenges for traditional banking institutions.\n\nHistorically, banks generated substantial income from: Wire transfers; Remittance services; International settlements; Payment processing fees.\n\nPayPal and similar platforms offer faster and often lower-cost alternatives, reducing traditional fee-based revenue streams and intensifying competition.\n\nAdditionally, the growing popularity of digital payments has reduced customer dependence on physical bank branches. Consumers increasingly prefer mobile applications and online platforms over branch visits for routine banking activities.\n\nAs a result, banks are compelled to: Restructure branch networks; Invest heavily in digital infrastructure; Strengthening cybersecurity systems; Enhance artificial intelligence and data analytics capabilities."
  },
  {
