    "chunk_text": "These rights ensure that dignity and professionalism guide every interaction between the Department and the public.\n\nAt the same time, the Charter sets out four key obligations. Taxpayers are expected to:\n\nThe positive impact of a Taxpayer Charter extends beyond legal clarity. It builds confidence. When taxpayers understand their rights, they feel secure. When they understand their obligations, they can comply with certainty. Clear communication reduces misunderstanding and promotes smoother transactions.\n\nThe Charter also strengthens accountability within the tax administration. By publicly committing to service standards, the Department reinforces professionalism, transparency, and consistency. This alignment between service and responsibility creates a stable environment for businesses and individuals alike.\n\nFor small and medium enterprises, clarity is particularly valuable. Predictable procedures help businesses plan finances, meet deadlines confidently, and focus on growth rather than uncertainty. For salaried taxpayers, clear rights provide reassurance that assessments and deductions are handled properly. For investors, a transparent tax framework enhances confidence in the overall economic environment. In this way, the Charter supports not only revenue collection but also economic stability.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s long-term development depends on sustainable domestic revenue mobilisation. Public services education, healthcare, infrastructure, and social protection are funded through taxation. A system built on fairness and mutual respect encourages voluntary compliance, which in turn strengthens revenue predictability.\n\nThe Taxpayer Charter plays a vital role in this process. By encouraging cooperation rather than confrontation, it fosters a culture of partnership between citizens and the State. This partnership is essential for national progress."
