    "chunk_text": "CLINICAL CLINCH: Patidar Blasts Bengaluru into IPL Final\n\nMay.27 (Mirror Sports) - Defending champions Royal Challengers Bengaluru stormed into the IPL final on Tuesday, crushing Gujarat Titans by 92 runs in a one-sided Qualifier 1 showdown.\n\nCaptain Rajat Patidar produced a sensational unbeaten 93 off just 33 balls, powering Bengaluru to 254-5 \u2014 the highest total ever recorded in an IPL playoff match.\n\n\u201cWe wanted an attacking mindset on this stage,\u201d Patidar said after earning Player of the Match honors. \u201cThe way we dominated was superb.\u201d\n\nVirat Kohli (43) and Devdutt Padikkal (30) laid the platform with a rapid 72-run stand before Jason Holder struck twice in one over.\n\nPatidar then exploded alongside Krunal Pandya (40), adding 95 runs as Gujarat\u2019s sloppy fielding unraveled. Patidar reached his fifty in just 21 balls.\n\nOpener Sai Sudharsan suffered a bizarre hit-wicket dismissal after losing grip of his bat, which crashed into the stumps.\n\nRasikh Salam struck twice in an over, while veterans Bhuvneshwar Kumar and Josh Hazlewood removed Shubman Gill and Jos Buttler early.\n\nA fighting 68 from impact substitute Rahul Tewatia delayed the inevitable, but Gujarat were bowled out for 162 in 19.3 overs.\n\nGujarat still have one final chance. Gill\u2019s side will face the winner of the Eliminator between Sunrisers Hyderabad and Rajasthan Royals on Friday for the remaining spot in the final."
