    "chunk_size_bytes": 1937,
    "chunk_text": "Israel says new head of Hamas\u2019 military wing killed in Gaza City strikes\n\nBBC - Israel says it has killed Hamas's armed wing commander Mohammed Odeh in a strike in Gaza on Tuesday - days after his predecessor died in a similar attack.\n\nAt least three Palestinians were killed and dozens more were injured in Tuesday's major attack, which targeted a residential building in one of Gaza City's busiest market areas, local medics and witnesses said.\n\nThe Israeli security agency, known as Shin Bet, and its military said in a statement that buildings that served as a hideout for Odeh were targeted after his movements were tracked for several months.\n\nIt is the latest deadly Israeli strike on Gaza despite a ceasefire with Hamas being in place.\n\nThe strike hit the upper three floors of the al-Kayali building in the centre of Gaza City, where streets were busy with shoppers ahead of the Muslim holiday Eid al-Adha.\n\nThe Israeli Defense Forces (IDF) and Shin Bet said: \"As part of the joint operation by the IDF and Shin Bet to eliminate the terrorist Muhammad Odeh, several buildings in the heart of Gaza City that served as a hideout for him were attacked, after months of intelligence surveillance in order to track his movements and the movements of his assistants in the organisation.\"\n\nThey added that that they had also struck \"a nearby apartment belonging to a Hamas terrorist who raided on October 7 and was part of Odeh's circle of assistants\".\n\nRescue teams rushed to the scene of the strikes but struggled to reach the upper floors because of the scale of the damage and congestion in the area.\n\nWitnesses said at least five missiles struck the building almost simultaneously from different directions.\n\nOne resident said he heard the sound of helicopter hovering overhead before the attack.\n\nFootage from the scene showed ambulances and civil defence crews searching through the damaged building as crowds gathered nearby."
  },
