    "chunk_text": "National Chamber and NEDA conduct \u2018Access to Finance Awareness Programme\u2019\n\nThe National Chamber of Commerce of Sri Lanka (NCCSL) and the National Enterprise Development Authority (NEDA) jointly hosted an \u201cAccess to Finance\u201d awareness programme on May 20, 2026, aimed at helping Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) secure concessionary loans. The event, held at the National Chamber Auditorium, featured Deputy Minister of Industry and Entrepreneurship Development, Chathuranga Abeysinghe, as the keynote speaker.\n\nTwo technical presentations followed: Kuloja G. Peiris (Acting Director, Department of Development Finance) outlined government concessionary support, while Jude T. Fernando (CEO, National Credit Guarantee Institution) discussed facilitating lending for SMEs lacking sufficient collateral. A panel discussion, moderated by NCCSL Secretary General Nilupul Chandrasena, explored key financing challenges and potential policy solutions. Panelists included representatives from NEDA, the Ministry of Finance, and Bank of Ceylon. The session concluded with an interactive Q&A.\n\nSri Lankan businesses interested in exploring potential trade partnerships with Indian counterparts can obtain detailed profiles of the delegates by contacting Nishanthi or Nethmi at 011 474 1788 / 076 255 5707 or via email at nishanthi@nationalchamber.lk or nethmi@nationalchamber.lk.\n\nRecovery trend catches on in stock trading; field day for bargain hunters\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
