    "chunk_text": "Initially entering the global market as a bulk tea exporter, ADRA Ceylon has built a strong foundation through its steadfast adherence to exemplary product quality, consistency, and strategic market expansion. Over the years, the company has progressively amplified its business model with a focus on value-added tea products to enhance brand presence and capture greater value within global markets.\n\nprofessionals, and a broader workforce of close to 350 across the Pink Eagle Group.\n\nADRA Ceylon\u2019s early years were characterized by rapid market penetration, followed by expanded brand development initiatives and substantial growth in value-added tea segments, positioning the company among the leading exporters of Ceylon tea to the region.\n\nFollowing its consolidation and entry into the export sector, the company rapidly expanded into the East Asian market by establishing a branch office in Taiwan during its second year of operations.\n\nIn its tenth year of operations, ADRA Ceylon successfully penetrated the highly competitive Gulf, UK, and French markets, further strengthening the company\u2019s presence across the Gulf region and Europe.\n\n\u201cADRA Ceylon\u2019s expansion over the past ten years reflects a meticulously executed global strategy. These achievements in global development have garnered industry recognition, including an honor at the NCE Export Awards in October 2019 for craft and commitment, a testament to ADRA\u2019s unyielding commitment,\u201d added Indika Abeywickrama, Director \u2013Tea. The company\u2019s international success is underpinned by several core strengths developed over its first decade. Meticulous sourcing from Sri Lanka\u2019s renowned tea regions, coupled with a rigorous \u201cleaf to cup\u201d quality control process ensures consistent premium quality."
