    "chunk_text": "The lobby upgrade reimagines the dramatic triple-height volume as a luxurious residential lounge rather than merely a transitional space. While preserving the openness, natural light, and restrained material palette of the original design, the new concept introduces curated seating clusters, textured rugs, marble tables, indoor planting, and vertical green features. These interventions create intimate pockets within the expansive volume, bringing warmth, comfort, and vibrancy to the interior environment.\n\n\u201cThe overall design intent was to create a more refined identity for Altair \u2014 one that feels welcoming during the day and visually striking in the evening. The upgrades bring together architecture, landscape, interiors, lighting, and branding into a cohesive and immersive experience,\u201d said Philip Weeraratne.\n\n\u201cThe renewed entrance and lobby environment was one of many new investments made after last year\u2019s purchase of Altair\u2019s parent company by Blackstone and is part of the vision of the new management to enhance the everyday experience of residents, strengthen the arrival impression for visitors, and thereby reinforce the property\u2019s lifestyle and hospitality-oriented character,\u201d affirmed Thilan Wijesinghe, Strategic Partner of Altair\u2019s owning company and Chairman of TWC Holdings.\n\nThe Community at Altair residence states that the lobby and entrance upgrades have infused Altair with renewed warmth, identity and sophistication."
