    "chunk_text": "The fourth quarter performance remained robust, despite the challenging operating conditions. Revenue for the quarter reached Rs.2.5 billion, representing a 46 percent increase, compared with Rs.1.7 billion recorded in the corresponding period last year.\n\nDMSL navigated the external pressures arising from the Middle East crisis, which contributed to higher domestic fuel prices and fuel rationing measures through QR code implementation.\n\nThe overall platform movements during the quarter increased 49 percent YoY, supported by record monthly unique consumers and stronger participation from independent third-party drivers.\n\nThe platform activity also rose 15 percent sequentially compared with the third quarter, which had experienced operational disruptions from Cyclone Ditwah.\n\nProfitability continued to strengthen during the quarter, with the operating profit rising 84 percent YoY to Rs.985 million, from Rs.534 million in the same period last year. The operating profit margin improved to 39 percent, up from 31 percent previously. The company attributed the improvement to stronger transaction volumes, pricing optimisation, higher operating leverage and cost management initiatives, particularly within the IT infrastructure.\n\nThe net profit after tax for the quarter climbed 86 percent to Rs.698 million, compared with Rs.375 million in the corresponding period of the previous financial year, while also recording a 26 percent quarter-on-quarter increase, reflecting sustained earnings momentum."
