    "description": "Swadeshi Khomba Baby Soap receives SLS certification",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/Swadeshi-Khomba-Baby-Soap-receives-SLS-certification/34-792601",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1779926787.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-05-28-dailyftlk-9b7f85b4-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "4a076903fc058397901e71dda599b8dd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1458,
    "chunk_text": "Swadeshi Khomba Baby Soap receives SLS certification\n\nSwadeshi Chief Executive Officer Amila Udawatte (centre left) receiving the SLS certification from Sri Lanka Standards Institution Director General/Chief Executive Officer Dr. Siddhika G. Senaratne whilst officials of Swadeshi Industrial Works and Sri Lanka Standards Institution look on\n\nSwadeshi Khomba Baby Soap has received the SLS certification issued by the Sri Lanka Standards Institution (SLSI).\n\nSwadeshi Deputy Chairperson/Managing Director Chulodhara Samarasinghe said by incorporating high-quality standards and processes, firmly certified under SLS, new parents can rest assured that their baby is in the safest natural nurturing care of Khomba Baby.\n\nSLS 547 is the Sri Lanka Standard Specification for Baby Soap, which sets mandatory quality, safety and performance requirements for soaps intended for infants. The SLS 547 standard includes requirements for ensuring baby soaps are safe, non-irritating, high quality, mild and suitable for infant skin. The standard is mandatory for both importation and local manufacturing, verified under the SLSI import inspection scheme.\n\nIn addition to the SLS 547 certification, Khomba Baby soap products have been internationally dermatologically tested and certified as safe for babies\u2019 skin. As a brand, Khomba Baby ensures compliance with the ISO 9001:2015 standard, thereby providing the best and safest quality herbal products in the country."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
