    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "ae68de78cb7bcf9766450883b21433d1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 861,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cThe Path of Freedom\u201d book launch tomorrow\n\nAn event to mark the launch of the book \u201cThe Path of Freedom: Dismantling the Imperialist Debt Trap,\u201d (de dollarization) will be held held tomorrow (29) at 3:30 p.m. at the Lavander Hall \u2013 BMICH.\n\nThe book, the latest by the author, Gayantha Dehiwatte, a graduate of Monash University, Melbourne, Australia, is an entrepreneur, Political Economic Analyst, and author of the book \u2018Wikalpa Maga\u2019, explores issues of economic sovereignty and the use of alternative currencies, such as the Chinese Yuan, for trade settlements and cross-border payments in order to reduce reliance on IMF-imposed conditions and avoid dependence on US dollar-denominated debt.\n\nSeveral members of the Diplomatic Corp in Colombo and Academia have been invited as guest. Members of the Press are encouraged to attend the launch."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-05-28-dailyftlk-a154e462",
    "num": "dailyftlk-a154e462",
    "date_str": "2026-05-28",
    "description": "\u2018From Friendship to Dependency\u2019 launched in Colombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/news/From-Friendship-to-Dependency-launched-in-Colombo/56-792604",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1779927375.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-05-28-dailyftlk-a154e462-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "701a7ad7dad2c0c7ae8b4d1d68435c45",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1975,
    "chunk_text": "\u2018From Friendship to Dependency\u2019 launched in Colombo\n\nFrom right: Panellists former Chief Hydrographer and maritime analyst Rear Admiral (Retd.) Y.N. Jayarathna,\u00a0University of Colombo Department of International Relations Head Dr. Pavithra Jayawardena, and former\u00a0Sri Lanka Navy Commander Admiral (Retd.) Jayanath Colombage in conversation with author Dr. Bhagya Senaratne\n\nAuthor Dr. Bhagya Senaratne (left) presenting a copy of the book to University of Colombo International Relations Emeritus Prof. Amal Jayawardena\n\nDR. Bhagya Senaratne launched her book From Friendship to Dependency: Analysing Sri Lanka\u2019s Foreign Policymaking Towards China at a recent event held at the Bandaranaike Centre for International Studies, Colombo.\n\nSpeaking at the event, Dr. Senaratne mentioned that her book examines why Sri Lanka\u2019s relations with China have been criticised for financial over-reliance and allegations of a \u2018debt trap.\u2019 She argues that these relations are deeply influenced by domestic political dynamics, including the roles of state leaders, foreign policy executives, and strategic culture.\n\nThe event also included a panel discussion, attended by former Commander of Sri Lanka Navy, Foreign Secretary and Ambassador of Sri Lanka Admiral Jayanath Colombage, Head of the Department of International Relations, University of Colombo Dr. Pavithra Jayawardena and former Chief Hydrographer and Maritime Analyst Rear Admiral Y.N. Jayarathna.\n\nAdmiral Colombage said: \u201cThis publications sheds light on Sri Lanka\u2019s locational importance and about the support Sri Lanka received at times when it was isolated in the international arena.\u201d\n\nIn her remarks, Dr. Jayawardena said: \u201cThis book is important in four key ways: it is rich in data compilations, offers a vast amount of ideas for future research prospects, is theoretically very rich as it focuses on Neoclassical Realism, and presents an alternative narrative, challenging dominant world views.\u201d"
  },
