    "chunk_text": "IMF approves USD 695 m tranche as Sri Lanka programme stays on track\n\nThe International Monetary Fund (IMF) Executive Board has approved the combined fifth and sixth reviews of Sri Lanka\u2019s Extended Fund Facility (EFF) arrangement, paving the way for the immediate disbursement of approximately USD 695 million, in a move widely seen as a strong endorsement of the country\u2019s ongoing economic recovery and reform agenda.\n\nThe latest approval brings total IMF financial support disbursed to Sri Lanka under the EFF programme to several billion dollars since the facility was launched in 2023 to stabilise the crisis-hit economy.\n\nDeputy Governor of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka Dr. Chandranath Amarasekara described the IMF Executive Board decision as a major milestone that demonstrates continued international confidence in Sri Lanka\u2019s macroeconomic reform programme.\n\n\u201cThis is another important step in Sri Lanka\u2019s economic stabilisation process. The successful completion of the reviews reflects the authorities\u2019 commitment to maintaining prudent macroeconomic policies, restoring fiscal discipline, strengthening governance and ensuring debt sustainability,\u201d Dr. Amarasekara said.\n\nHe noted that the IMF-backed reforms had already contributed significantly towards restoring macroeconomic stability, rebuilding investor confidence and improving the country\u2019s external sector performance.\n\nEconomic analysts say the approval is expected to further strengthen market confidence at a time when Sri Lanka is gradually emerging from its worst economic crisis in decades, characterised by sovereign default, foreign exchange shortages and soaring inflation.\n\nOfficials pointed out that the country has recorded notable improvements in key economic indicators, including easing inflation, stabilisation of the exchange rate, improved foreign reserve levels and renewed confidence in the banking and financial sectors."
