    "chunk_text": "Officials pointed out that the country has recorded notable improvements in key economic indicators, including easing inflation, stabilisation of the exchange rate, improved foreign reserve levels and renewed confidence in the banking and financial sectors.\n\nDr. Amarasekera expressed appreciation to IMF officials Evan Papageorgiou, Martha Tesfaye Woldemichael and the IMF staff for their continued engagement and close collaboration with Sri Lanka during the review process.\n\nSpecial commendation was also extended to Dr. Sujeetha Jegajeevan, Sri Lanka\u2019s Alternate Executive Director at the IMF, for representing the country at the Executive Board discussions.\n\nEconomists believe the latest tranche would provide further support for Sri Lanka\u2019s balance of payments position while helping sustain critical reforms aimed at achieving long-term economic resilience and inclusive growth.\n\nThe IMF\u2019s latest decision is also likely to boost investor sentiment and support ongoing negotiations linked to debt restructuring and international financing cooperation.\n\nBOI unveils \u2018Ready to Invest\u2019 platform to drive next wave of foreign investment\n\n365 Future Energy explores sustainable energy investment opportunities in Sri Lanka\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
