    "chunk_text": "BOI unveils \u2018Ready to Invest\u2019 platform to drive next wave of foreign investment\n\nIn a bold move aimed at accelerating foreign direct investment and positioning Sri Lanka as a leading investment destination in the Indian Ocean region, the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka (BOI) has launched its flagship digital investment platform, \u201cReady to Invest,\u201d offering global investors direct access to 30 structured, project-ready ventures across some of the country\u2019s most strategic sectors.\n\nThe platform, now live at readytoinvestsl.com\u2060, is expected to serve as a one-stop gateway for international investors seeking immediate entry into Sri Lanka\u2019s rapidly recovering economy.\n\nThe projects featured on the platform span eight high-potential sectors \u2014 Tourism and Leisure, Manufacturing, Transport and Logistics, ICT, Innovation and Tech Park Development, Agriculture and Agro Processing, Urban, Residential and Mixed-use Development, Aviation, Ports and Maritime Infrastructure, and Renewable Energy and Sustainability.\n\nThe launch comes amid growing international confidence in Sri Lanka\u2019s economic recovery following sweeping fiscal and structural reforms undertaken in recent years.\n\nActing Chairman of the BOI, Dr. Sulakshana Jayawardena, described the initiative as a transformational step in Sri Lanka\u2019s investment promotion strategy, noting that the country was now moving decisively from recovery to growth.\n\nHe said the \u201cReady to Invest\u201d initiative was designed to eliminate traditional investment bottlenecks by presenting investors with bankable, implementation-ready projects backed by policy support and institutional facilitation.\n\nInvestment officials said Sri Lanka\u2019s economic fundamentals have shown remarkable resilience, with the country recording 5.0 percent GDP growth in both 2024 and 2025, signalling sustained recovery momentum."
