    "chunk_text": "Investment officials said Sri Lanka\u2019s economic fundamentals have shown remarkable resilience, with the country recording 5.0 percent GDP growth in both 2024 and 2025, signalling sustained recovery momentum.\n\nThe BOI also disclosed that nearly USD 1.9 billion worth of BOI-approved projects are now ready to break ground, potentially generating thousands of jobs and stimulating economic activity across multiple sectors.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s investor-friendly regulatory framework continues to be a major attraction, with 100 percent foreign ownership permitted in most sectors and full repatriation of capital and profits guaranteed.\n\nOfficials further highlighted Sri Lanka\u2019s strategic location along one of the world\u2019s busiest maritime trade routes, its highly literate and English-speaking workforce, and expanding infrastructure network as key advantages for global businesses seeking regional operational hubs.\n\nEconomic observers say the launch of the \u201cReady to Invest\u201d platform signals a new phase in Sri Lanka\u2019s economic diplomacy, with the country aggressively courting high-quality foreign investments capable of driving exports, technology transfer, innovation, and sustainable development.\n\nAnalysts also noted that the initiative reflects a growing urgency within policymakers to convert economic stabilisation into tangible growth, employment creation, and long-term investor partnerships.\n\nWith Sri Lanka now actively showcasing ready-to-launch projects rather than merely promoting potential opportunities, the BOI\u2019s latest initiative is widely viewed as a strategic attempt to reposition the country as a competitive and credible destination for global capital.\n\nTokyo Cement posts strong FY2025/26 Q4 performance amid intense cost pressures\n\nIMF approves USD 695 m tranche as Sri Lanka programme stays on track\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comm