    "chunk_text": "Over 200 models and 50+ designers audition for Sri Lanka\u2019s first Women\u2019s Fashion Week\n\nThe Ceylon Chamber of Women Entrepreneurs (CCWE) held its Model & Designer Open Call at the City of Dreams CMB, Colombo, in a landmark step toward Sri Lanka\u2019s first-ever fashion week dedicated exclusively to women entrepreneurs. The auditions drew more than 200 models including a wave of fresh faces making their industry debut alongside over 50 designers eager to claim a spot on the runway.\n\nTwo separate panels of expert judges assessed the participants. The Designer Panel comprised Prof. (Mrs) Samudrika Wijayapala, Ms. Kanchana Perera, Jagjit Silva, Kalum Udawaththa, Roshan Peris and Nilushi Pawanya. The Model Panel featured Dannielle Kerkoven Fernando, Sanjeewani Embuldeniya, Dineth De Silva, Manoji Wadugodapitiya, Kamil Hewavitharana, and Svitlana Melnyk (Lana) bringing a combined depth of local and international fashion expertise to the auditions. Celebrated choreographer Gihan Dassanayake, who will lead the runway choreography at the main event, was also in attendance.\n\n\u201cThis Open Call is an invitation to every woman who has dared to dream. The response today is a testament to the incredible talent across Sri Lanka. CCWE Fashion Week 2026 will be a platform that transforms aspirations into opportunity.\u201d\n\nUnderstanding the influence of Traffic Light Labelling and Pricing on the demand for sugar sweetened beverages in Sri Lanka\n\nAitken Spence Printing achieves historic milestone with WorldStar 2026 win for Sri Lanka\u2019s offset printing industry\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
