    "md5": "1b18e9e9bc41d334a069867e33d47334",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1745,
    "chunk_text": "LG launches first-ever business innovation centre in Sri Lanka at Abans\n\nLG Electronics marked a historic milestone in the Sri Lankan commercial technology landscape with the grand opening of its first-ever LG Business Innovation Centre at Abans on 14th May 2026. The centre is the country\u2019s first experience hub dedicated exclusively to advanced Information Displays and Audio-Visual (AV) solutions.\n\nThe inauguration ceremony was graced by a host of distinguished dignitaries, including LG Sri Lanka Managing Director Keith Chung; Abans Managing Director Rusi Pestonjee; Abans Director Dr. Saroshi Dubash; and , Abans Director Business Development Tanaz Pestonjee.\n\nUnlike traditional retail outlets, the new centre is designed to offer visitors a comprehensive and immersive understanding of LG\u2019s commercial capabilities. Rather than showcasing isolated products, the facility presents complete, integrated solutions, allowing businesses to experience firsthand how LG\u2019s technology can transform their operations.\n\nThis centre positions Abans and LG at the forefront of digital transformation in Sri Lanka, providing innovative solutions that foster smarter, more flexible business environments.\n\nVisitors to the Innovation Centre can explore a wide array of flagship LG products, including Video Walls, Digital Signage, All-in-One LED Screens and the smart LG CreateBoard.\n\nThe centre also highlights how LG drives innovation across specific sectors such as retail through LG\u2019s Retail Signage Solutions, creating engaging in-store experiences using vivid digital displays. These are powered by smart management tools such as SuperSign CMS and LG ConnectedCare, allowing businesses to manage content remotely and ensure system uptime."
  },
