    "md5": "50b7db75b660a86c22f90161d7885fca",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1509,
    "chunk_text": "Aitken Spence Printing achieves historic milestone with WorldStar 2026 win for Sri Lanka\u2019s offset printing industry\n\nDirector / Chief Executive Officer Deshantha Silva (right),\u00a0 receiving the award at the WorldStar awards ceremony held in Germany\n\nAitken Spence Printing has achieved a landmark international recognition by becoming the first and only offset printing company in Sri Lanka to win an award at the prestigious WorldStar Awards, organised by the World Packaging Organisation (WPO). The Company secured the WorldStar 2026 Award for Packaging Excellence in the Luxury Packaging category, reaffirming Sri Lanka\u2019s growing capability in world-class printing and packaging innovation.\n\nThe award was presented at the WorldStar Awards Ceremony in May 2026, in D\u00fcsseldorf, held alongside Interpack; the world\u2019s leading trade fair for processing and packaging technologies, bringing together global industry leaders and innovators.\n\nWidely regarded as one of the highest accolades in the global packaging industry, the WorldStar Awards are open exclusively to winners of recognised national or regional packaging competitions.\n\nThe World Packaging Organisation, a non-profit, non-governmental international federation, brings together packaging institutes, associations, corporations, and trade organisations from around the world under its mission of \u201cBetter quality of life through better packaging for more people.\u201d The organisation currently comprises 84 members representing 66 countries."
