    "chunk_text": "The World Packaging Organisation, a non-profit, non-governmental international federation, brings together packaging institutes, associations, corporations, and trade organisations from around the world under its mission of \u201cBetter quality of life through better packaging for more people.\u201d The organisation currently comprises 84 members representing 66 countries.\n\nFurther commenting on this achievement, Aitken Spence PLC Chairperson Stasshani Jayawardena said: \u201cThis recognition at the WorldStar Awards is a proud milestone not only for Aitken Spence Printing, but also for Sri Lanka\u2019s manufacturing and export sectors as a whole. It reflects the ability of Sri Lankan enterprises to compete and succeed on the global stage, displaying innovation, quality, sustainability, and operational excellence. I am delighted that the team at Aitken Spence Printing has been recognised for continuously raising industry benchmarks and reinforcing the Group\u2019s commitment to delivering internationally recognised products and services.\u201d\n\nWith a legacy spanning more than 7 decades, Aitken Spence Printing has evolved from an in-house printing operation in Galle into one of Sri Lanka\u2019s leading full-service printing and packaging providers, catering to both local and international markets. The Company serves a diverse portfolio of sectors including FMCG, tea, beverage and tobacco, pharmaceuticals, publications, consumer durables, apparel, stationery and point-of-sale materials (POSM).\n\nOperating from its state-of-the-art 100,000-square-foot manufacturing facility in Mawaramandiya, just outside Colombo, the Company continues to invest in cutting-edge printing technologies and operational excellence to meet evolving customer needs."
