    "chunk_size_bytes": 903,
    "chunk_text": "Woman dies after three-wheeler crashes into bus stop in Thambalagamuwa\n\nColombo, May 29 (Daily Mirror) - A woman has died and three others were injured after a three-wheeler veered off the road and crashed into a bus stop along the Kantale\u2013Trincomalee Road in the Thambalagamuwa Police Division yesterday (28).\n\nPolice said the accident occurred near Vaulpalama when the three-wheeler, which was travelling from Kantale towards Trincomalee, reportedly veered off the road after the driver fell asleep.\n\nThe vehicle then collided with a bus stop, injuring the driver and three women who were seated in the rear.\n\nAll injured persons were admitted to the Thambalagamuwa Hospital, where one of the women succumbed to her injuries.\n\nThe deceased was identified as a 70-year-old resident of the Galmatiya area.\n\nPolice in the Thambalagamuwa Division are conducting further investigations into the incident."
