    "chunk_text": "Special trains to operate for Vesak pilgrims\n\nColombo, May 29 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0 The Railway Department has announced the operation of several special train services on May 30 and 31 to facilitate travel during the Vesak Full Moon Poya holidays.\n\nThe department said the special services are being introduced to ease transportation for devotees travelling to Anuradhapura and for members of the public attending the State Vesak Festival at the ancient Raja Maha Vihara in Thihagoda, Midellawela in Matara.\n\nRailway officials said the additional train services will operate throughout the two-day Vesak period in view of the anticipated increase in passenger demand.\n\nThe Railway Department has announced that several special train services will operate from May 30 \u2013 31 to facilitate travel during the Vesak Full Moon Poya.\n\nAccording to the department, the services are aimed at easing travel for devotees heading to Anuradhapura and for the public attending the State Vesak Festival at the ancient Raja Maha Vihara in Thihagoda, Midellawela, in Matara."
