    "chunk_size_bytes": 1825,
    "chunk_text": "Prime Land Residencies exits financial biz following sale of 400 million HNB Finance shares\n\nThe CSE recorded satisfactory turnover yesterday when Prime Land Residencies sold 400 million shares of HNB Finance for Rs 3.5 billion by way of a crossing or arranged transaction.\n\nHowever, the actual buyer in this transaction was not revealed but Prime Lands Residencies exited the financial business after this divestiture.\n\nAmid of those developments the day\u2019s turnover stood at more than Rs 7 billion. The All Share Price Index went up by 127.75 points while S and P SL20 rose by 37.16 points. Turnover stood at Rs 7.38 billion with eight crossings.\n\nThose crossings were; HNB Finance 400 million shares crossed for Rs 3 5 billion; its shares traded at Rs 8.80, Softlogic Life 10.8 million shares crossed for Rs 1 billion; its shares traded at Rs 92, TJ Lanka two million shares crossed for Rs 63 million; its shares traded at Rs 31.60, JKH 3.1 million shares crossed for Rs 62.9 million; its shares traded at Rs 20, Dialog Axiata 1.1 million shares crossed for Rs 48 million; its shares sold at Rs 41.80, CDB (Non-Voting) one million shares crossed for Rs 33.5 million; its shares sold at Rs 33.50 and CIP Holdings one million shares crossed for Rs 33 million; its shares sold at Rs 33.\n\nIn the retail market companies that mainly contributed to the turnover were; HNB Rs 374 million (945,000 shares traded), Commercial Bank Rs 270 million (1.3 million shares traded), HNB Finance Rs 161 million (16.4 million shares traded), Sampath Bank Rs 119 million (839,000 shares traded), Access Engineering Rs 111 million (1.4 million shares traded), JKH Rs 109 million (5.4 million shares traded) and Softlogic Life Rs 90 million (950,000 shares traded). During the day 516 million share volumes changed hands in 23906 transactions."
