    "md5": "f5e47d0e7993c99b3fe4515b5a7bb749",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1738,
    "chunk_text": "Vesak-poya, Thoughts II \u2013 Meditation- an acquired Skill\n\nThe best seller book, \u2018The Selfish Gene\u2019, by Richard Dawkins revolutionized evolutionary biology by shifting the perspective of survival, from organism-centered to gene-centered, long-term survival of genetic information. Survival and reproduction, hence remains the core driving force for natural selection-adapting to the environment, in evolution of all life-forms.\n\nSurvival is the key for all life-forms, including humans. In Buddhist phrenology- (terms)- \u2018Bhava-Tanha\u2019. It is a natural Force. Could it be, if Samsara exists \u2013 natures mechanism to keep life-forms on Earth, or projected further, in the Universe! Survival entails acts of Kamma. Intrusion into your personal space (inclusive of \u2018I\u2019 or narrative me \u2013 (i.e. reputation, achievements) or that of family or tribal space etc., would provoke in the untrained human Mind, reactions -intentions (Cetana) \u2013 creating unwholesome Kamma. It could be argued that, that Kammic-Force, which through Dependent\u2013Origination (Paticca-Samuppada), is nature\u2019s way of sustaining life-forms in the Universe \u2013 ie. sustains Samsara.\n\nHumans are accustomed to introspection-ruminating on past \u2018baggage\u2019, memories etc., in most of their free moments. Functional Magnetic Imaging (fMRI), scans show the Default Mode Network (DMN), is the major neuronal network (See Fig: across), wherein in which much of DMN activity occurs. In contrast the Task based network, the Central Executive Network, is activated in living in the \u2018now\u2019. Mindfulness Meditation is in the latter category. Persistent, prolonged meditation has been shown to suppress the DMN. Making the Mind transcend from a mere State to a Trait."
  },
