    "description": "Power cuts Imposed to maintain grid stability: Minister",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/breaking-news/Power-cuts-Imposed-to-maintain-grid-stability-Minister/108-341585",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1780133242.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-05-30-dailymirrorlk-39ef44af-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "8bb5309f72f400c0e1fafa445ab0a1c2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1192,
    "chunk_text": "Power cuts Imposed to maintain grid stability: Minister\n\nElectricity supply was temporarily disconnected in nearly 100 areas, including parts of Colombo, due to an imbalance in the national power grid,\u00a0Power and Energy Minister Anura Karunathilaka said.\n\nThe Minister explained that the measure was taken to ensure the stability of the electricity system after power generation exceeded demand as a result of higher-than-anticipated solar power generation.\n\nHe noted that recent rainy weather conditions had led authorities to expect lower levels of solar generation. However, clear skies and strong sunlight today resulted in a significant amount of electricity being generated through rooftop solar systems and fed into the national grid.\n\nAccording to the Minister, the situation has primarily affected areas in the Western Province, where rooftop solar installations are concentrated, including Kalutara and Panadura.\n\nHe further stated that the temporary power interruptions were implemented as a precautionary measure to prevent the risk of a major islandwide blackout.\n\nThe Minister added that electricity supply is expected to be fully restored between 2.00 p.m. and 3.00 p.m. today."
  },
