    "chunk_size_bytes": 1716,
    "chunk_text": "La Trobe Forum examines AI\u2019s impact on future jobs\n\nLa Trobe University, Colombo, in collaboration with Study Melbourne, Victoria, Australia, and La Trobe University, Australia, recently held a panel discussion on \u201cAI and Future Employment Opportunities,\u201d bringing together academics, education leaders and industry experts to examine how artificial intelligence is reshaping the global workforce.\n\nThe event, held at La Trobe University Colombo, focused on the evolving role of AI in employment, with discussions centred on emerging career pathways, digital skill requirements, automation trends, ethical considerations, and the transformation of business and healthcare sectors.\n\nParticipants included school principals, teachers, and higher education professionals, who shared perspectives on how students and educators can prepare for a rapidly changing job market driven by technological advancement.\n\nDistinguished guests at the event included Michelle Wade, Victoria\u2019s Commissioner to South Asia, Global Victoria, State Government of Victoria, Australia; David Walker, Associate Dean, Learning & Teaching, La Trobe Business School; Louise Lexis, Associate Dean, School of Agriculture, Biomedicine and Environment; Lisa Ritchie, Lecturer, School of Psychology and Public Health; Amit Malhotra, Senior Regional Director (South Asia and Africa); and Piyush Wahi, Associate Director (South Asia and Africa), La Trobe University.\n\nSpeaking at the forum, Michelle Wade highlighted the importance of collaboration between education providers and industry stakeholders in equipping students with the skills needed to navigate opportunities emerging from artificial intelligence and the changing world of work."
