    "chunk_text": "Union Assurance agency premier league celebrates sport and fellowship\n\nUnion Assurance, the country\u2019s longest-standing private life insurer, brought together its agency network in a celebration of sport and camaraderie with the staging of the Union Assurance Agency Premier League for the second consecutive year at the NCC Grounds.\n\nThe event drew more than 900 participants, including senior management of the agency business, and featured competition alongside community engagement under the banner of sport and fellowship.\n\nPart of the company\u2019s agent value proposition, the Premier League is designed to promote holistic well-being, professional development, internal community building and long-term engagement across its nationwide agency network.\n\nTeams representing Union Assurance\u2019s islandwide agency divisions competed in both male and female categories. This year\u2019s edition was extended beyond the field of play, with agents joined by their families, transforming the tournament into a wider social gathering. A dedicated children\u2019s carnival added colour to the event, providing entertainment for younger attendees.\n\nSenior leadership from the agency division also took part, underscoring the organisation\u2019s emphasis on agent recognition and engagement.\n\nIn the men\u2019s category, Team Chilaw of the North Western 01 Zone emerged champions, while Victory Queens of the Uva-Central Zone secured the women\u2019s title. Both teams were awarded the Union Assurance Agency Premier League trophy, a perpetual shield that will be defended annually as the tournament builds its legacy.\n\nChief Agency Officer Imtiyaz Aniff said the event reflected the camaraderie and unity within the agency force, noting that the inclusion of families added a deeper dimension to the gathering.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website